                    {
                        "translation_id": "1930beb2-41d7-4f3c-8a40-4a9dd00f8984",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a6cd61b-7780-3cb8-90ed-fe2625b2a66b",
                        "source_sense_id": "245faf11-8be8-3479-98dd-5be8dfc1561b",
                        "target_lang_word": "cashew",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cashew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7714356-fa19-31a4-aac7-a335ce2f081f",
                                        "entry_id": "36018b7b-7696-3901-b624-36eb8ce272d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tree, Anacardium occidentale, native to northeastern Brazil, now widely grown in tropical climates for its cashew nuts and cashew apples."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70eccadc-75af-4dc3-87b8-bedf06b3ba4c",
                                                "sense_id": "a7714356-fa19-31a4-aac7-a335ce2f081f",
                                                "text": "Also known as the Native Cashew, it is a member of the Anacardiaceae, the same plant family to which the Cashew and Mango trees belong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55e680bf-492c-46d6-b972-4a7d538b615e",
                                                "sense_id": "a7714356-fa19-31a4-aac7-a335ce2f081f",
                                                "text": "Cashew (Anacardium occidental L.) is an export-oriented crop grown for its nuts, a true drupe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1b27525-0061-48c3-b089-c09aec6a1648",
                                                "sense_id": "a7714356-fa19-31a4-aac7-a335ce2f081f",
                                                "text": "Soft-wood grafting and veneer grafting are successful in cashew."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe911d20-d50e-3452-aa0e-edd6cc037c90",
                                        "entry_id": "36018b7b-7696-3901-b624-36eb8ce272d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cashew nut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32ed59fd-486d-4d75-b81d-d082855aa18d",
                                                "sense_id": "fe911d20-d50e-3452-aa0e-edd6cc037c90",
                                                "text": "In some countries, cashews continue to be cracked manually although cracking machinery and other shelling mechanisms have been introduced."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80d49595-8c43-4f5a-99e5-ec5120939c76",
                                                "sense_id": "fe911d20-d50e-3452-aa0e-edd6cc037c90",
                                                "text": "The bland cashew is a fitting substitute for higher priced almonds to extend the nut texture. In baking, however, almonds are more suitable for cake decoration than cashews."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d3d5b7d-1a8d-403f-ac53-3486a4ce1fb7",
                                                "sense_id": "fe911d20-d50e-3452-aa0e-edd6cc037c90",
                                                "text": "This is a spicy variation of Kung Pao Chicken using cashews rather than the more common peanuts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfeda36e-2361-4a6b-9807-2949831c9ac8",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a6cd61b-7780-3cb8-90ed-fe2625b2a66b",
                        "source_sense_id": "245faf11-8be8-3479-98dd-5be8dfc1561b",
                        "target_lang_word": "anacardier",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anacardier",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f33dc5b2-9222-3d4a-9cc3-cb5d59e12121",
                                        "entry_id": "0e6bcb50-ac45-3675-bcb3-cfc9cfcf3848",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Arbre du genre Anacardium originaire des régions tropicales d’Amérique, pouvant atteindre 12 mètres de haut et dont l'espèce Anacardium occidentale donne un fruit nommé noix de cajou."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fe9e5bb-d46a-4d86-866c-3f3510477bfa",
                                                "sense_id": "f33dc5b2-9222-3d4a-9cc3-cb5d59e12121",
                                                "text": "Le fruit de l’anacardier est appelé pomme de cajou, il est consommé frais en Amérique latine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea9777cb-4a7b-4184-aa03-3f10280dcc0b",
                                                "sense_id": "f33dc5b2-9222-3d4a-9cc3-cb5d59e12121",
                                                "text": "L’intégration de l’anacardier dans l’assolement est récente dans les régions baoulé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11007ad9-d0a1-4cfd-9a30-4b0fb1be8692",
                                                "sense_id": "f33dc5b2-9222-3d4a-9cc3-cb5d59e12121",
                                                "text": "l’anacardier (Anacardium occidentale) … donne la noix de cajou. Il s’agit d’un arbre de 10 à 15 mètres aux feuilles épaisse et ovoïdes. Le fruit, ou pomme de cajou, est rougeâtre à maturité et renferme une noix réniforme contenue dans un péricarpe à trois couches. La couche centrale est remplie d’une huile brunâtre composée d’acide anacardique et de cardol, chimiquement apparentée à l’urushiol et également allergisante. L’huile est utilisée pour la fabrication de garniture de freins et d’embrayages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
